I'm away from my computer at the moment, so this might not very be very helpful, but I know folks have done some things with occupancy modeling of salamanders that are occasionally below ground and unavailable for sampling. Your situation is also somewhat analogous to occupancy modeling with camera traps where animals may be present in the study area, but not within range of the camera, and thus are unavailable for sampling. It might be worthwhile looking into camera trap models, too.

